            <div xml:id="d970">

                <pb facs="1300" n="1176" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg1176"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">467.11 W 89/26: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the High Commissioner at Constantinople</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-09-25T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 25,
                                1923—5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>173. Your telegram 249 of September 23. Authority is granted for you to resume
                    negotiations to seek an arrangement for the settling of claims in accordance
                    with the plans which have been approved in our 149, August 8, 2 p.m., via
                    Lausanne or in the various instructions which were sent to the Special Mission
                    at Lausanne.</p>
                <p>An answer will soon be sent to your telegram 240 of September 15.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
